\[
n_i = \sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\theta_i^{\,k}
    = \frac{\theta_i}{1-\theta_i}, \qquad i=A,B.
\]

Hence  

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
n_A &= \frac{\theta_A}{1-\theta_A},\\[4pt]
n_B &= \frac{\theta_B}{1-\theta_B},
\end{aligned}
}
\]

and the total film thickness follows  

\[
\boxed{
h = n_A\,\delta_A + n_B\,\delta_B
  = \frac{\theta_A}{1-\theta_A}\,\delta_A
    + \frac{\theta_B}{1-\theta_B}\,\delta_B .
}
\]

