**Derivation**

1. **Adsorption equilibria**

\[
\begin{aligned}
K_{AH}&=\frac{\theta_{AH}}{p_{AH}\,\theta_*}
\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\theta_{AH}=K_{AH}\,p_{AH}\,\theta_*\\[4pt]
K_{O_2}&=\frac{\theta_O^{2}}{p_{O_2}\,\theta_*^{2}}
\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\theta_O=\sqrt{K_{O_2}\,p_{O_2}}\;\theta_*\\[4pt]
K_{H_2O}&=\frac{\theta_{H_2O}}{p_{H_2O}\,\theta_*}
\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\theta_{H_2O}=K_{H_2O}\,p_{H_2O}\,\theta_*
\end{aligned}
\]

2. **Site balance**

\[
\theta_*+\theta_{AH}+\theta_O+\theta_{H_2O}=1
\]

Insert the expressions from step 1:

\[
\theta_* \Bigl[1+K_{AH}p_{AH}+\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}+K_{H_2O}p_{H_2O}\Bigr]=1
\]

Hence

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle 
\theta_*=\frac{1}{1+K_{AH}p_{AH}+\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}+K_{H_2O}p_{H_2O}}}
\]

3. **Coverages of the reacting species**

\[
\begin{aligned}
\theta_{AH}&=K_{AH}p_{AH}\,\theta_*
      =\frac{K_{AH}p_{AH}}
            {1+K_{AH}p_{AH}+\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}+K_{H_2O}p_{H_2O}}\\[4pt]
\theta_O&=\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}\,\theta_*
      =\frac{\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}}
            {1+K_{AH}p_{AH}+\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}+K_{H_2O}p_{H_2O}}
\end{aligned}
\]

4. **Surface‑reaction rate (per catalytic site)**  

The rate‑determining step is

\[
\text{AH}^*+\text{O}^*\;\xrightarrow{k_r}\;\text{CO}_2+\text{H}_2\text{O}+2*
\]

Thus the rate per surface site is

\[
r_s=k_r\,\theta_{AH}\,\theta_O
   =k_r\,
     \frac{K_{AH}p_{AH}\,\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}}
          {\bigl[1+K_{AH}p_{AH}+\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}+K_{H_2O}p_{H_2O}\bigr]^2}
\]

5. **Conversion to a volumetric rate**

For a cylindrical monolith of radius \(R\) and length \(L\),

\[
\frac{\text{catalyst surface area}}{\text{reactor volume}}
   =\frac{2\pi RL}{\pi R^{2}L}= \frac{2}{R}\equiv a_s
\]

Hence the volumetric reaction rate is

\[
r_{AH}=a_s\,r_s
      =\frac{2}{R}\,
        k_r\,
        \frac{K_{AH}p_{AH}\,\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}}
             {\bigl[1+K_{AH}p_{AH}+\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}+K_{H_2O}p_{H_2O}\bigr]^2}
\]

---

\[
\boxed{\,r_{AH}
   =\frac{2\,k_r\,K_{AH}\,\sqrt{K_{O_2}}\;p_{AH}\,\sqrt{p_{O_2}}}
          {R\Bigl[\,1+K_{AH}p_{AH}+\sqrt{K_{O_2}p_{O_2}}+K_{H_2O}p_{H_2O}\Bigr]^{2}}\,}
\]

This expression gives the volumetric rate of aromatic‑hydrocarbon oxidation on the CNF‑metal coated monolithic catalyst, accounting for competitive adsorption of water vapor.

