**Derivation**

Let \(\theta_{*}\) denote the fraction of vacant vacancy sites.  
For each adsorbate \(i\) (\(i=\mathrm{SO_{2}},\;\mathrm{H_{2}O},\;\mathrm{O_{2}}\)) the Langmuir adsorption equilibrium gives  

\[
K_{i}\;=\;\frac{\theta_{i}}{p_{i}\,\theta_{*}}
\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad
\theta_{i}=K_{i}\,p_{i}\,\theta_{*}.
\]

The site‑balance on the surface is  

\[
\theta_{*}+ \theta_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}+ \theta_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}}+ \theta_{\mathrm{O_{2}}}=1 .
\]

Substituting the expressions for \(\theta_{i}\) gives  

\[
\theta_{*}+ \bigl(K_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}p_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}
+K_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}}p_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}}
+K_{\mathrm{O_{2}}}p_{\mathrm{O_{2}}}\bigr)\theta_{*}=1,
\]

so that  

\[
\theta_{*}= \frac{1}{1+K_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}p_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}
+K_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}}p_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}}
+K_{\mathrm{O_{2}}}p_{\mathrm{O_{2}}}} .
\]

Finally, each fractional coverage follows from \(\theta_{i}=K_{i}p_{i}\theta_{*}\):

\[
\theta_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}= \frac{K_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}\,p_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}}
{1+K_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}\,p_{\mathrm{SO_{2}}}
+K_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}}\,p_{\mathrm{H_{2}O}}
+K_{\mathrm{O_{2}}}\,p_{\mathrm{O_{2}}}},
\]

