**Derivation**

1. **Quasi‑equilibrated adsorption steps**  

\[
\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{CO(g)}+* &\rightleftharpoons \mathrm{CO*}\qquad 
K_{\rm CO}= \frac{\theta_{\rm CO}}{P_{\rm CO}\,\theta_*}
\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\theta_{\rm CO}=K_{\rm CO}\,P_{\rm CO}\,\theta_*\\[4pt]
\mathrm{H_2O(g)}+* &\rightleftharpoons \mathrm{H_2O*}\qquad 
K_{\rm H_2O}= \frac{\theta_{\rm H_2O}}{P_{\rm H_2O}\,\theta_*}
\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\theta_{\rm H_2O}=K_{\rm H_2O}\,P_{\rm H_2O}\,\theta_*
\end{aligned}
\]

2. **Site balance** – because the OH* and H* species are generated in the RDS and consumed in the very fast steps 4 and 5, their steady‑state coverages are much smaller than those of CO*, H₂O* and vacant sites.  Hence we approximate  

\[
C_s=\theta_*+\theta_{\rm CO}+\theta_{\rm H_2O}
\]

Substituting the expressions from (1),

\[
C_s=\theta_* \bigl[1+K_{\rm CO}P_{\rm CO}+K_{\rm H_2O}P_{\rm H_2O}\bigr]
\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\theta_*=\frac{C_s}{1+K_{\rm CO}P_{\rm CO}+K_{\rm H_2O}P_{\rm H_2O}}
\]

and

\[
\theta_{\rm H_2O}=K_{\rm H_2O}P_{\rm H_2O}\,\theta_*=
\frac{C_s\,K_{\rm H_2O}P_{\rm H_2O}}
{1+K_{\rm CO}P_{\rm CO}+K_{\rm H_2O}P_{\rm H_2O}} .
\]

3. **Rate‑determining step (step 3)**  

\[
\mathrm{H_2O*}+* \;\xrightarrow{k_3}\; \mathrm{OH*}+ \mathrm{H*}
\]

\[
r\equiv -\frac{dF_{\rm CO}}{dW}=k_3\,\theta_{\rm H_2O}\,\theta_*
