The grand‑canonical probability of a microstate with \(N\) CO₂ molecules at positions \(\{{\bf r}_i,\Omega_i\}\) is  

\[
\pi(N,\mathbf X_N)=\frac{1}{\Xi}\,
\frac{z^{N}}{N!\,\Lambda^{3N}}\,
\exp\!\big[-\beta U_N(\mathbf X_N)\big],
\qquad 
z=e^{\beta\mu},
\]

with \(U_N=U_{\rm LJ}+U_{\rm Coul}\).  
For an insertion we propose a new molecule at a random position \({\bf r}_{\rm new}\) and orientation \(\Omega_{\rm new}\); the reverse deletion chooses one of the \(N+1\) molecules uniformly.  Detailed balance gives  

\[
P_{\rm ins}
=\min\Bigl[1,\,
\frac{\pi(N+1)}{\pi(N)}\,
\frac{p_{\rm del}}{p_{\rm ins}}\Bigr]
=\min\Bigl[1,\,
\frac{V}{(N+1)\Lambda^{3}}\,
\exp\!\big[\beta\mu-\beta\Delta U\big]\Bigr],
\]

where \(\Delta U=U_{N+1}-U_{N}\).  Splitting the energy change into Lennard‑Jones and Coulomb parts,

\[
\Delta U=\Delta U_{\rm LJ}+\Delta U_{\rm Coul}.
\]

The Coulomb contribution of the inserted CO₂ molecule interacting with the disordered framework charges is  

\[
\Delta U_{\rm Coul}
=
\underbrace{\sum_{i\in{\rm frame}}
\sum_{\alpha\in{\rm CO_2}}
\frac{q_f^{\,i}\,q_{\rm CO_2}^{\,\alpha}}
{4\pi\varepsilon_0\,r_{i\alpha}}}_{\text{framework–CO$_2$}}
\;+\;
\underbrace{\sum_{j=1}^{N}
\sum_{\alpha\in{\rm CO_2}}
\sum_{\beta\in{\rm CO_2}_j}
\frac{q_{\rm CO_2}^{\,\alpha}\,q_{\rm CO_2_j}^{\,\beta}}
{4\pi\varepsilon_0\,r_{\alpha\beta}}}_{\text{CO$_2$–CO$_2$}} .
\]

The set of framework charges \(\{q_f^{\,i}\}\) reflects the random Si substitution:  

\[
q_f^{\,i}= 
\begin{cases}
 -e & \text{Al tetrahedral site},\\[2pt]
 0   & \text{Si‑substituted site (probability }x\text{)},\\[2pt]
 +e & \text{extra‑framework cation (e.g., H$^+$) placed to neutralise each Al}.
\end{cases}
\]

Thus the Metropolis acceptance probability for inserting a CO₂ molecule is  

\[
\boxed{
P_{\rm ins}
=\min\Bigl\{1,\,
\frac{V}{(N+1)\Lambda^{3}}\,
\exp\!\big[\beta\mu-\beta\Delta U_{\rm LJ}
-\beta\Delta U_{\rm Coul}\big]\Bigr\},
}
\]

with \(\Delta U_{\rm Coul}\) given above.  The corresponding deletion probability follows from detailed balance:

\[
\boxed{
P_{\rm del}
=\min\Bigl\{1,\,
\frac{N\Lambda^{3}}{V}\,
\exp\!\big[-\beta\mu+\beta\Delta U_{\rm LJ}
+\beta\Delta U_{\rm Coul}\big]\Bigr\}.
}
\]

