            =\frac{m_{\text{beads}}}{\rho_{\text{glass}}}\,
              \frac{3}{r_{\text{bead}}}
            =\frac{6\,m_{\text{beads}}}{\rho_{\text{glass}}\,d_{\text{bead}}}\;,
\]

with \(d_{\text{bead}}=50\;\mu\text{m}=5.0\times10^{-3}\,\text{cm}\) and \(r_{\text{bead}}=d_{\text{bead}}/2\).

The amine sites contributed by silane A are \(f_A\sigma_{\text{total}}A_{\text{total}}\) and those from silane B are \((1-f_A)\sigma_{\text{total}}A_{\text{total}}\).  All amine sites can react with glutaraldehyde, so the number of template molecules immobilized is  

\[
\begin{aligned}
