The free‑energy change for a circular nucleus containing \(n\) molecules is  

\[
\Delta G(n)= -n\Delta\mu+\gamma L(n),\qquad 
L(n)=2\pi r,\qquad 
n=\frac{\pi r^{2}}{a_{0}} .
\]

From the geometric relation  

\[
r=\sqrt{\frac{a_{0}n}{\pi}}\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
L(n)=2\pi\sqrt{\frac{a_{0}n}{\pi}}
      =2\sqrt{\pi a_{0}}\;n^{1/2}.
\]

Hence  

\[
\Delta G(n)= -\Delta\mu\,n+2\gamma\sqrt{\pi a_{0}}\;n^{1/2}.
\]

The critical nucleus size follows from the extremum condition  

\[
\frac{\partial\Delta G}{\partial n}=0
\;\Longrightarrow\;
-\Delta\mu+\gamma\sqrt{\pi a_{0}}\;n^{-1/2}=0 .
\]

Solving for \(n\) gives  

\[
n^{*}= \left(\frac{\gamma\sqrt{\pi a_{0}}}{\Delta\mu}\right)^{2}
      =\frac{\pi a_{0}\gamma^{2}}{\Delta\mu^{2}} .
\tag{1}
\]

The chemical‑potential difference depends on the surface coverage,
\[
\Delta\mu=\Delta\mu_{0}\bigl(\theta-\theta_{c}\bigr),
\qquad
\theta(T,p)=\frac{K(T)p}{1+K(T)p},
\qquad
K(T)=K_{0}\exp\!\Bigl(\frac{E_{\rm ads}}{k_{\!B}T}\Bigr).
\]

Thus  

\[
\Delta\mu
   =\Delta\mu_{0}\!\left[\frac{K_{0}e^{E_{\rm ads}/(k_{\!B}T)}\,p}
                               {1+K_{0}e^{E_{\rm ads}/(k_{\!B}T)}\,p}
                               -\theta_{c}\right].
\tag{2}
\]

Substituting (2) into (1) yields the explicit critical nucleus size

\[
\boxed{
n^{*}
   =\frac{\pi a_{0}\,\gamma^{2}}
          {\Delta\mu_{0}^{\,2}\,
           \Bigl[\displaystyle 
                 \frac{K_{0}\,e^{E_{\rm ads}/(k_{\!B}T)}\,p}
                      {1+K_{0}\,e^{E_{\rm ads}/(k_{\!B}T)}\,p}
                 -\theta_{c}\Bigr]^{2}}
}
\]

(defined only for \(\theta>\theta_{c}\); otherwise \(n^{*}\to\infty\)).  

The corresponding critical radius follows from \(r^{*}=\sqrt{a_{0}n^{*}/\pi}\):

\[
\boxed{
r^{*}
   =\frac{a_{0}\,\gamma}
          {\Delta\mu_{0}\,
           \Bigl[\displaystyle 
                 \frac{K_{0}\,e^{E_{\rm ads}/(k_{\!B}T)}\,p}
                      {1+K_{0}\,e^{E_{\rm ads}/(k_{\!B}T)}\,p}
                 -\theta_{c}\Bigr]}
}
\]

These expressions give the critical nucleus size (or radius) as a function of temperature \(T\), vapor pressure \(p\), and the model parameters \(E_{\rm ads},K_{0},\Delta\mu_{0},\theta_{c},\gamma,a_{0}\).

