\;=\;
\int_{0}^{t_b}\!\big(F_{\rm in,o}-F_{\rm out,o}\big)\,dt
\;=\;
(1-\alpha)\,y_{o}\,\dot n_{\rm tot}\;t_b ,
\]

where  

* \(q_{\rm eq}=K_{H,o}\,P_{o}=K_{H,o}\,y_{o}P_{\rm tot}\)  (Henry’s law),  
* \(F_{\rm in,o}=y_{o}\,\dot n_{\rm tot}\)  (inlet molar flow of o‑xylene),  
* \(F_{\rm out,o}= \alpha\,y_{o}\,\dot n_{\rm tot}\)  at breakthrough (\(\alpha=0.05\)),  
* \(\dot n_{\rm tot}=Q_{\rm STP}/V_{m,\rm STP}\)  (total molar flow, with \(V_{m,\rm STP}=22.414\;{\rm L\,mol^{-1}}\)).  

Solving for the breakthrough time gives  

\[
t_{b,o-x}
= \frac{M_{\rm ads}\,K_{H,o}\,y_{o}P_{\rm tot}}
{(1-\alpha)\,y_{o}\,\dot n_{\rm tot}}
= \frac{M_{\rm ads}\,K_{H,o}\,P_{\rm tot}}
{(1-\alpha)\,\dot n_{\rm tot}}
= \frac{M_{\rm ads}\,K_{H,o}\,P_{\rm tot}\,V_{m,\rm STP}}
{(1-\alpha)\,Q_{\rm STP}} .
\]

Hence, for the given data (\(\alpha=0.05\))  

\[
\boxed{t_{b,o-x}= \frac{M_{\rm ads}\,K_{H,o}\,P_{\rm tot}}{0.95\,\dot n_{\rm tot}}
      = \frac{M_{\rm ads}\,K_{H,o}\,P_{\rm tot}\,V_{m,\rm STP}}{0.95\,Q_{\rm STP}} } .
\]

