    -T\big(\Delta S_{\rm vib}+ \Delta S_{\rm rot}+ \Delta S_{\rm trans}\big) .
\end{aligned}
}
\]

where for each species \(i\)

\[
\begin{aligned}
ZPE_i &=\sum_{j}\frac{1}{2}h\nu_{ij},\\[2pt]
U_{\rm vib}^i &=\sum_{j}\Big[\frac{h\nu_{ij}}{2}+
          \frac{h\nu_{ij}}{e^{h\nu_{ij}/k_{\!B}T}-1}\Big],\\[2pt]
S_{\rm vib}^i &=R\sum_{j}\Big[\frac{h\nu_{ij}/k_{\!B}T}
          {e^{h\nu_{ij}/k_{\!B}T}-1}
          -\ln\!\big(1-e^{-h\nu_{ij}/k_{\!B}T}\big)\Big],\\[4pt]
U_{\rm rot}^{\rm CH_4}&=RT,\qquad 
S_{\rm rot}^{\rm CH_4}=R\Big[\ln\!\Big(\frac{T^{3/2}}{\sigma\theta_A\theta_B\theta_C}\Big)+\tfrac32\Big],\\[2pt]
U_{\rm trans}^{\rm CH_4}&=\tfrac32RT,\qquad 
S_{\rm trans}^{\rm CH_4}=R\Big[\ln\!\Big(\big(\tfrac{2\pi mk_{\!B}T}{h^2}\big)^{3/2}\frac{k_{\!B}T}{p}\Big)+\tfrac52\Big],\\[4pt]
U_{\rm trans}^{\rm ads}&=RT,\qquad 
S_{\rm trans}^{\rm ads}=R\Big[\ln\!\Big(\tfrac{2\pi mk_{\!B}T}{h^2}A\Big)+1\Big],
\end{aligned}
\]

with \(m\) the molecular mass, \(A\) the surface area per adsorption site, 
\(\sigma\) the symmetry number, and \(\theta_{A,B,C}=h\nu_{A,B,C}/k_{\!B}\) the characteristic rotational temperatures.  

The Ga–O–Zeolite framework is treated as a surface species; it contributes only vibrational (and, if desired, hindered‑rotational) terms, i.e. \(U_{\rm trans}^{\rm Ga\!-\!O}=0\) and \(S_{\rm trans}^{\rm Ga\!-\!O}=0\).  

Thus the activation free energy at 298 K is obtained by evaluating the electronic DFT energies of the transition state and the reactants and adding the zero‑point, thermal vibrational, rotational and translational corrections as shown above.

