The isoelectric point is reached when the effective surface potential vanishes,  

\[
\psi_{\rm eff}=0\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\psi_{0}= \frac{z\,e\,\Gamma_{\rm surf}}{C_{s}} .
\]

Hence the surface coverage required for charge neutralisation is  

\[
\Gamma_{\rm req}= \frac{\psi_{0}C_{s}}{z\,e}.
\]

The specific capacitance of the diffuse layer is  

\[
C_{s}= \frac{\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}}{\lambda_{D}},\qquad 
\lambda_{D}= \Bigl(\frac{\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}k_{B}T}{2N_{A}e^{2}I}\Bigr)^{1/2}
      =\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}k_{B}T}{2N_{A}e^{2}I}} .
\]

Thus  

\[
C_{s}= \frac{\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}}
            {\sqrt{\displaystyle\frac{\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}k_{B}T}
                                 {2N_{A}e^{2}I}}}
      =\sqrt{\frac{2N_{A}\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}I\,e^{2}}{k_{B}T}}
      =e\sqrt{\frac{2N_{A}\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}I}{k_{B}T}} .
\]

The required coverage becomes  

\[
\Gamma_{\rm req}= \frac{\psi_{0}}{z}\,
                  \sqrt{\frac{2N_{A}\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}I}{k_{B}T}} .
\]

The adsorbed amount follows the Langmuir isotherm  

\[
\Gamma_{\rm surf}= \frac{\Gamma_{\max}K(M)C_{p}}
                        {1+K(M)C_{p}},\qquad 
K(M)=k_{2}M^{\beta}.
\]

Setting \(\Gamma_{\rm surf}= \Gamma_{\rm req}\) and solving for the polymer
concentration gives  

\[
\Gamma_{\rm req}\bigl[1+K(M)C_{p}^{*}\bigr]
      =\Gamma_{\max}K(M)C_{p}^{*}
\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
C_{p}^{*}= \frac{\Gamma_{\rm req}}
                {K(M)\bigl[\Gamma_{\max}-\Gamma_{\rm req}\bigr]} .
\]

Substituting \(\Gamma_{\rm req}\) and \(K(M)\) yields the explicit expression

\[
\boxed{
C_{p}^{*}= 
\frac{\displaystyle\frac{\psi_{0}}{z}
      \sqrt{\frac{2N_{A}\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}I}{k_{B}T}}}
     {\displaystyle k_{2}M^{\beta}
      \Bigl[\Gamma_{\max}
            -\frac{\psi_{0}}{z}
             \sqrt{\frac{2N_{A}\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}I}{k_{B}T}}
      \Bigr]}
}
\]

or, equivalently,

\[
C_{p}^{*}= 
\frac{\psi_{0}}{z\,k_{2}M^{\beta}}\;
\frac{\displaystyle\sqrt{\frac{2N_{A}\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}I}{k_{B}T}}}
     {\displaystyle\Gamma_{\max}
      -\frac{\psi_{0}}{z}
       \sqrt{\frac{2N_{A}\varepsilon\varepsilon_{0}I}{k_{B}T}}}\; .
\]

**Remark.** In the present planar‑capacitor model the polymer‑layer thickness
\(\delta(M)=k_{1}M^{\alpha}\) does not enter the condition \(\psi_{\rm eff}=0\);
consequently the constants \(k_{1}\) and \(\alpha\) cancel out of the
isoelectric‑point expression.

