The surface reaction (step 3) is the only irreversible step, so at steady state the CO₂ formation rate per surface site is  

\[
r_{\mathrm{CO}_2}=k_{\rm r}\,\theta_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm O}.
\]

---

### 1.  Quasi‑equilibrium adsorption steps  

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{CO(g)}+* &\rightleftharpoons \text{CO*} &
\Longrightarrow\qquad 
K_{\rm CO}&=\frac{\theta_{\rm CO}}{p_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm vac}}
\;\;\Rightarrow\;\;
\boxed{\theta_{\rm CO}=K_{\rm CO}\,p_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm vac}}\\[4pt]
\text{O}_2(g)+2* &\rightleftharpoons 2\text{O*} &
\Longrightarrow\qquad 
K_{\rm O_2}&=\frac{\theta_{\rm O}^2}{p_{\rm O_2}\,\theta_{\rm vac}^2}
\;\;\Rightarrow\;\;
\boxed{\theta_{\rm O}= \sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}\,p_{\rm O_2}}\;\theta_{\rm vac}} .
\end{aligned}
\]

---

### 2.  Site balance  

\[
\theta_{\rm CO}+\theta_{\rm O}+\theta_{\rm vac}=1 .
\]

Insert the expressions for \(\theta_{\rm CO}\) and \(\theta_{\rm O}\):

\[
K_{\rm CO}p_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm vac}
+\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}p_{\rm O_2}}\,\theta_{\rm vac}
+\theta_{\rm vac}=1 .
\]

Hence  

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle 
\theta_{\rm vac}= \frac{1}
{1+K_{\rm CO}p_{\rm CO}+\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}p_{\rm O_2}}}} .
\]

From this we obtain the coverages

\[
\theta_{\rm CO}= \frac{K_{\rm CO}p_{\rm CO}}
{1+K_{\rm CO}p_{\rm CO}+\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}p_{\rm O_2}}},\qquad
\theta_{\rm O}= \frac{\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}p_{\rm O_2}}}
{1+K_{\rm CO}p_{\rm CO}+\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}p_{\rm O_2}}}.
\]

---

### 3.  Steady‑state rate law  

\[
\begin{aligned}
r_{\mathrm{CO}_2}
&=k_{\rm r}\,\theta_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm O}  \\
&=k_{\rm r}\,\bigl(K_{\rm CO}p_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm vac}\bigr)
\bigl(\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}p_{\rm O_2}}\,\theta_{\rm vac}\bigr)\\[4pt]
&=k_{\rm r}\,K_{\rm CO}\,\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}}\;
p_{\rm CO}\,\sqrt{p_{\rm O_2}}\;
\theta_{\rm vac}^{\,2}.
\end{aligned}
\]

Substituting \(\theta_{\rm vac}\) gives the explicit LH rate expression:

\[
\boxed{
r_{\mathrm{CO}_2}=k_{\rm r}\,K_{\rm CO}\,\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}}\;
p_{\rm CO}\,\sqrt{p_{\rm O_2}}\;
\left[\frac{1}
{1+K_{\rm CO}p_{\rm CO}+\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}p_{\rm O_2}}}\right]^{\!2}
}.
\]

If the rate is required per unit surface area, the site density \(N_{\rm S}\) can be introduced as a multiplicative factor, i.e.  

\[
r_{\mathrm{CO}_2}=k_{\rm r}\,N_{\rm S}\,
\frac{K_{\rm CO}\,\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}}\;p_{\rm CO}\,\sqrt{p_{\rm O_2}}}
{\bigl(1+K_{\rm CO}p_{\rm CO}+\sqrt{K_{\rm O_2}p_{\rm O_2}}\bigr)^{2}} .
\]

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{CO adsorption:}\qquad &K_{\mathrm{CO}}
      =\frac{\theta_{\mathrm{CO}}}{p_{\mathrm{CO}}\;\theta_{\mathrm{vac}}}
      \;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
      \theta_{\mathrm{CO}} = K_{\mathrm{CO}}\,p_{\mathrm{CO}}\;\theta_{\mathrm{vac}} ,\\[4pt]
\text{O}_{2}\text{ dissociative adsorption:}\qquad 
      &K_{\mathrm{O}_{2}}
      =\frac{\theta_{\mathrm{O}}^{\,2}}{p_{\mathrm{O}_{2}}\;\theta_{\mathrm{vac}}^{\,2}}
      \;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
      \theta_{\mathrm{O}} = \sqrt{K_{\mathrm{O}_{2}}\,p_{\mathrm{O}_{2}}}\;\theta_{\mathrm{vac}} .
\end{aligned}
\]

With the site‑balance \(\theta_{\mathrm{CO}}+\theta_{\mathrm{O}}+\theta_{\mathrm{vac}}=1\),

\[
\theta_{\mathrm{vac}}\Bigl[1+K_{\mathrm{CO}}p_{\mathrm{CO}}+\sqrt{K_{\mathrm{O}_{2}}p_{\mathrm{O}_{2}}}\Bigr]=1,
\qquad
\theta_{\mathrm{vac}}=
\frac{1}{\,1+K_{\mathrm{CO}}p_{\mathrm{CO}}+\sqrt{K_{\mathrm{O}_{2}}p_{\mathrm{O}_{2}}}\,}.
\]

Hence the fractional coverages are

\[
