Here \(\beta=1/(k_{\!B}T)\), \(\Lambda\) is the thermal de Broglie wavelength of water, \(\mathbf{C}=\{\mathbf{R}_{j},q_{j}\}\) denotes the fixed cation positions and charges (Na⁺ or Ca²⁺), \(U_{\mathrm{ww}}\) is the TIP4P/2005 water–water potential, \(U_{\mathrm{wf}}\) the water–framework interaction, and  

