The interaction potential is obtained from  

\[
U(D)=-\int_{D}^{\infty}F(D')\,\mathrm dD'\qquad\bigl[U(\infty)=0\bigr].
\]

---

### 1.  Van der Waals term  

\[
F_{\text{vdW}}(D)=-\frac{A_{H}R}{6D^{2}}
\]

\[
\begin{aligned}
U_{\text{vdW}}(D)&=-\int_{D}^{\infty}\!\!\Bigl(-\frac{A_{H}R}{6D'^{2}}\Bigr)\,\mathrm dD'   
= \frac{A_{H}R}{6}\int_{D}^{\infty}D'^{-2}\,\mathrm dD'\\[2pt]
&=\frac{A_{H}R}{6}\Bigl[-\frac{1}{D'}\Bigr]_{D}^{\infty}
=-\frac{A_{H}R}{6D}\; .
\end{aligned}
\]

---

### 2.  Electrostatic double‑layer term  

\[
F_{\text{EDL}}(D)=\frac{64\pi R k_{\!B}T\,n_{0}\,\gamma^{2}}{\kappa}\,e^{-\kappa D}
\]

\[
\begin{aligned}
U_{\text{EDL}}(D)&=-\int_{D}^{\infty}\frac{64\pi R k_{\!B}T\,n_{0}\,\gamma^{2}}{\kappa}
\,e^{-\kappa D'}\;\mathrm dD'\\[2pt]
&=-\frac{64\pi R k_{\!B}T\,n_{0}\,\gamma^{2}}{\kappa}
\Bigl[-\frac{1}{\kappa}e^{-\kappa D'}\Bigr]_{D}^{\infty}\\[2pt]
&= \frac{64\pi R k_{\!B}T\,n_{0}\,\gamma^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\,e^{-\kappa D}\; .
\end{aligned}
\]

---

### 3.  Steric term  

\[
F_{\text{steric}}(D)=A\,Q^{2}\,e^{-D/L}
\]

\[
\begin{aligned}
U_{\text{steric}}(D)&=-\int_{D}^{\infty}A\,Q^{2}\,e^{-D'/L}\,\mathrm dD'\\[2pt]
&=-A Q^{2}\Bigl[-L\,e^{-D'/L}\Bigr]_{D}^{\infty}
= A L Q^{2}\,e^{-D/L}\; .
\end{aligned}
\]

---

### 4.  Total interaction potential  

Adding the three contributions:

\[
\boxed{%
U_{\text{tot}}(D)=
-\frac{A_{H}R}{6\,D}
+\frac{64\pi R k_{\!B}T\,n_{0}\,\gamma^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\,e^{-\kappa D}
+ A\,L\,Q^{2}\,e^{-D/L}
}
\]

By construction \(U_{\text{tot}}(\infty)=0\). This expression gives the total interaction potential energy as a function of the separation distance \(D\) for the silica probe–substrate system.

