The elementary WGS rate per Cu surface site is  

\[
r \;=\;k\,\theta_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm OH}\qquad\bigl[\text{mol\,s}^{-1}\text{ per Cu site}\bigr].
\]

Multiplying by the number of Cu surface sites present in one gram of catalyst, \(N_{\rm Cu}\) (sites g⁻¹), gives the observable rate per gram of catalyst  

\[
r_g \;=\;k\,\theta_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm OH}\;N_{\rm Cu}.
\]

Because the intrinsic rate constant scales with Cu dispersion,  

\[
k \;=\;k_0\,D_{\rm Cu},
\]

the expression becomes  

\[
r_g \;=\;k_0\,D_{\rm Cu}\,N_{\rm Cu}\,\theta_{\rm CO}\,\theta_{\rm OH}.
\]

The coverages follow the Langmuir–Hinshelwood forms (competitive adsorption on Cu sites only):  

\[
\theta_{\rm CO}
   =\frac{K_{\rm CO}P_{\rm CO}}
          {1+K_{\rm CO}P_{\rm CO}+K_{\rm H_2O}P_{\rm H_2O}+K_{\rm O_2}P_{\rm O_2}},
\qquad
\theta_{\rm OH}
   =\frac{K_{\rm H_2O}'P_{\rm H_2O}}
          {1+K_{\rm H_2O}'P_{\rm H_2O}} .
\]

Substituting these coverages gives the steady‑state WGS rate per gram of catalyst:

\[
\boxed{
r_g
   = k_0\,D_{\rm Cu}\,N_{\rm Cu}\;
     \frac{K_{\rm CO}\,P_{\rm CO}}
