\[
\begin{aligned}
\eta(\dot\gamma_c)&=\eta_0=K\,\dot\gamma_c^{\,n-1},\\[4pt]
\eta(\dot\gamma_{\rm ref})&=\eta_{\rm ref}=K\,\dot\gamma_{\rm ref}^{\,n-1}.
\end{aligned}
\]

Dividing the two relations gives  

\[
\frac{\eta_{\rm ref}}{\eta_0}
=\Bigl(\frac{\dot\gamma_{\rm ref}}{\dot\gamma_c}\Bigr)^{\,n-1}
\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
n-1=\frac{\ln(\eta_{\rm ref}/\eta_0)}{\ln(\dot\gamma_{\rm ref}/\dot\gamma_c)},
\]

so that  

\[
\boxed{\,n=1+\frac{\ln\!\big(\eta_{\rm ref}/\eta_0\big)}
               {\ln\!\big(\dot\gamma_{\rm ref}/\dot\gamma_c\big)}\,}.
\]

The consistency index follows from either of the two equations, e.g.  

\[
\boxed{\,K=\frac{\eta_0}{\dot\gamma_c^{\,n-1}}
       =\frac{\eta_{\rm ref}}{\dot\gamma_{\rm ref}^{\,n-1}}\,}.
\]

